sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as User
  participant GM as GatewayModal.jsx
  participant PB as POST /payments/intents
  participant GW as Mock gateway: POST /gateway/confirm
  participant WH as deliver_webhook() in gateway.py
  participant DB as SQLite
  participant ML as mailer.py
  participant OD as GET /orders/ID
  GM->>PB: createIntent(orderId)
  PB->>DB: INSERT payment_intent (amount from the order, client_secret)
  PB-->>GM: intentId and clientSecret
  U->>GM: card or UPI details
  GM->>GW: intentId, clientSecret, details
  GW->>GW: judge(): validate format, test cards decline
  GW->>GW: build event and sign it with HMAC-SHA256
  GW->>WH: raw body and X-Gateway-Signature header
  WH->>WH: verify the signature (constant time)
  WH->>DB: load intent and order
  WH->>WH: amount equals order total? intent still open?
  alt payment.succeeded
    WH->>DB: order paid, paid_at set (shipping clock starts)
    WH->>ML: confirmation email as a background task
  else payment.failed
    WH->>DB: order failed (customer can retry)
  end
  GW-->>GM: succeeded or failed plus a message (not proof)
  loop up to 8 times
    GM->>OD: is paymentStatus paid yet?
  end
  GM-->>U: success, open the order page
  Note over GM,DB: A real gateway calls the webhook over HTTP from its own servers. Unpaid after 15 minutes: the order is cancelled and stock released.
